  "name": "Beko (southern Malagasy vocal polyphony)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Beko is the funeral song of the Antandroy (Tandroy) of the dry far south of Madagascar: an a cappella polyphony, usually of two or three voices, in which a lead singer improvises verses recounting the deceased's genealogy, character and passions while the others sustain an accompanying part. Its specialist singers, the mpibeko, sing in a high register with a deliberately nasal, trembling timbre, partly stopping an ear with a finger to monitor the voice.",
